course: dictionary
lesson: 14076
title: Meaningful
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Meaningful» has a few meanings, and the words around it show which one is meant. «Her sentence was meaningful, every word made sense.» Here it means clear. «Lunch with my grandad is meaningful to me» shows it means important to someone.
explain: Read the clues. «He gave me a meaningful look across the room.» Nobody spoke, so the look must carry a hidden feeling or thought without words. In maths or science, «a meaningful difference» means a difference big enough to be real, not just luck.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try a simple swap such as clear, important, or real, and check the sentence still works. If it does, you have found the meaning.
fact: Meaningful means having a clear meaning, or being important or valuable to someone.
fact: «A meaningful sentence» is one that makes sense.
fact: «A meaningful look» shows a hidden feeling or thought without words.
fact: In science and maths, «a meaningful difference» is big enough to be real, not just chance.
fact: Phrases like «meaningful conversation» and «make it meaningful» describe talk or action that matters.
exercise: «The gift was meaningful to her, because it came from her best friend.» What does meaningful mean here? | *Important to someone | Wrapped in paper | Cheap and quick to buy | Very heavy
exercise: «He gave me a meaningful look.» What does the look show? | *A hidden feeling without words | A sneeze | A loud shout | A question about the time
exercise: Maths: «The new fertiliser made a meaningful difference to the plant's growth.» What does meaningful suggest? | *Big enough to be real, not just chance | Very small and hard to see | Happening at the same time | Brightly coloured
test: «Every word in her story was meaningful, so it made sense from start to finish.» What does meaningful mean here? | *Having a clear meaning | Very long | Full of pictures | Hard to read
test: Ella says, «We had a meaningful chat about our hopes.» What does meaningful chat suggest? | A chat with no words | *A chat that matters to them | A chat about the weather only | A chat that is loud and fast
exam: Which sentence uses meaningful to mean making sense? | I had a meaningful dream about the sea | Meaningful is a colour | *The story had a meaningful ending that made sense | The meaningful dog barked all night
